      "id": "1336",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1336,
        "relationship_type": "synonym",
        "body": "を marks the direct object, the thing an action is done to (e.g., リンゴを食べた = '[I] ate an apple'). に has multiple functions, including marking the destination of movement or the target of an action. Be aware that grammar patterns can differ between English and Japanese: for example, 'I passed the test' uses 試験に合格する in Japanese, not 試験を合格する.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 32,
          "slug": "に",
          "title": "に",
          "meaning": "In, At, To, For, On",
          "level": "JLPT5",
